```console
kettle-jem
K_JEM_TEMPLATING=true kettle-jem install
K_JEM_TEMPLATING=true kettle-jem selftest
```

`kettle-jem` setup creates or updates `.structuredmerge/kettle-jem.yml`,
installs template support, and runs the template workflow. `kettle-jem install`
reapplies full template updates and regenerates local finishing artifacts such
as binstubs.
Use `kettle-jem template --only PATH` for scoped file updates. `kettle-jem
selftest` checks template drift in a temporary workspace. The `kettle:jem:*`
rake tasks are internal targets used by the executable after it prepares the
templating environment.

Useful runtime controls:

| Setting | Use |
|---|---|
| `KETTLE_JEM_VERBOSE=true` | Show detailed template output. |
| `PARSE_ERROR_MODE=fail` | Fail when an AST/parser-backed merge cannot run. |
| `PARSE_ERROR_MODE=skip` | Preserve the destination when parsing is unavailable. |
| `FAILURE_MODE=error` | Raise on merge failure. |
| `FAILURE_MODE=rescue` | Warn and keep unmerged content on merge failure. |
| `only=glob,glob` | Limit the template run to matching paths. |
| `include=glob,glob` | Add matching paths to the run. |
| `hook_templates=l|g|n` | Install local hooks, global hooks, or no hooks. |
| `git_drivers=semantic-diff|builtin-diff|global|include-file|check|undo|none` | Install, verify, remove, or skip StructuredMerge Git diff driver setup. |
